; ======================================================================
;  hw_id_q.pi4 - Arduino UNO Q HwId backend: WHAT THIS COMPUTER IS.
;
;  Forum 575. This board is the one the defect was found on: run against
;  a core that stated the Pi 4's facts as literal prose, the first line
;  this monitor ever printed on real Q silicon said it was a Raspberry
;  Pi 4, named a PL011 at 00000000 that does not exist here, and asserted
;  exception level 2 on a processor sitting at EL1.
;
;  The board file answered that by carrying its own QBanner() and its own
;  CmdQVersion(), with a comment saying in as many words that the core
;  hard-coding one board's facts was a real defect in the core and was not
;  fixed from there. Both are gone now: the core asks, this file answers,
;  and a third board answers for itself rather than inheriting whichever
;  board happened to be written first.
;
;  INCLUDE ORDER: after Board/qefi_q.pi4 (the loaded-image record),
;  Board/hwinfo_q.pi4 (HwInfoEl), Core/format.pi4 (PutAddr), and before
;  Core/flow_cmd.pi4 and Core/help.pi4, which are the two callers.
; ======================================================================

Procedure.i HwIdBoard()
  ProcedureReturn "Arduino UNO Q"
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwIdCpu()
  ProcedureReturn "Cortex-A53"
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwIdTarget()
  ProcedureReturn "unoq"
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  HwIdEl() - READ, never assumed. This is the value that made the case:
;  the core printed the digit 2 and CurrentEL on this board reads 0x4,
;  which is EL1. HwInfoEl() (Board/hwinfo_q.pi4) decodes bits 3:2 of the
;  register, so the banner states what the running processor is, and a
;  firmware that one day handed the app a different level would move the
;  printed number with it instead of quietly contradicting it.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i HwIdEl()
  ProcedureReturn HwInfoEl()
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  HwIdSayConsole() - there is no serial port on this bench, and saying
;  so is most of what an operator needs from this paragraph: they are
;  reading it out of a log file on a disk, not off a wire, and the reason
;  is a 1.8 V header they cannot reach.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure HwIdSayConsole()
  PrintN("The console is the firmware's own: UEFI Simple Text Output and Input,")
  PrintN("with boot services still up. There is no UART in it - the GENI SE4 is")
  PrintN("1.8 V and unreachable on this bench - so the session transcript is")
  PrintN("written to \EFI\anvil\anvil.log on the EFI System Partition, which")
  PrintN("is where anyone reading this is reading it from.")
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  HwIdSayImage() - the image contract, which is the half of `version`
;  that really is different between the two boards. The A64 backend is
;  the SAME one, and saying so is the point: somebody who reads "unoq"
;  and goes looking for a second code generator will not find one.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure HwIdSayImage()
  PrintN("  The A64 backend is the same one the Pi 4 uses, because the A53 and")
  PrintN("  the A72 are both ARMv8.0-A. Only the image contract differs: this is")
  PrintN("  an AArch64 UEFI application, entered with boot services up, and not")
  PrintN("  a kernel8.img.")
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  HwIdImageBase() / HwIdImageLen() - forum 586, the content stamp.
;
;  On this board the firmware chooses where the image goes and how much
;  of it there is, and it will say so: EFI_LOADED_IMAGE_PROTOCOL carries
;  ImageBase and ImageSize, which Board/qefi_q.pi4 reads back at run time.
;  That is why the answer here is measured rather than constant, and why
;  a firmware that refuses to answer gets a 0 and an honest sentence
;  instead of a guessed extent - the same rule `boot` already follows on
;  this board when it refuses every payload for want of the same record.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i HwIdImageBase()
  If QEfiImageKnown() = 1
    ProcedureReturn QEfiImageBase()
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure

Procedure.i HwIdImageLen()
  If QEfiImageKnown() = 1
    ProcedureReturn QEfiImageSize()
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  HwIdSayImageWhere() - and here the provenance carries a WARNING as
;  well as a source, which is why it runs to four lines and why the seam
;  lets the board PRINT it instead of returning one long fragment.
;
;  The digest the core computes from this extent is over the image AS
;  UEFI LOADED IT, not over the file on the EFI System Partition: a PE
;  loader relocates and pads, so the two are not the same bytes, and
;  comparing this number against a host-side digest of the .efi file
;  would fail on a perfectly good image. It still tells two builds apart,
;  which is what 586 asked for, and this says exactly that much and no
;  more - a digest offered as more than it is would be the confident
;  wrong answer in a new place.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure HwIdSayImageWhere()
  If QEfiImageKnown() = 1
    PrintN("  That extent is the firmware's own loaded-image record, so the digest")
    PrintN("  covers the image AS LOADED and not the file on the EFI System")
    PrintN("  Partition - a PE loader relocates and pads. It tells two builds")
    PrintN("  apart; it will NOT match a host-side digest of the .efi file.")
    ProcedureReturn
  EndIf
  PrintN("  The firmware would not say where it loaded this image. That is the")
  PrintN("  same answer that makes boot refuse every payload on this board, and")
  PrintN("  it is the safe direction: an extent this monitor cannot prove is one")
  PrintN("  it will not hash.")
EndProcedure
